{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And you shall purge the innocent blood.</b> Its meaning: the punishment for the innocent blood. Or it may be: \"the blood\" — the blood of the innocent. And some say: you are obligated to purge [the shedding of] blood. And the correct interpretation in my eyes is what I have mentioned, that no innocent blood be shed in your land if you do what is right in the eyes of YHWH, according to the secret: the reward for a transgression is a transgression, and the reward for a commandment is a commandment."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:07.785060466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}